{"type":"message","id":"65d48b2f","parentId":"35375dcd","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:39:55.117Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The image key is a placeholder \"img_v1_xxx\" which is not a real file key. The actual image from the message isn't visible in the metadata. \n\nSince I can't see the actual image content in this message, I should tell 频哥我准备好了，让女儿把图片发过来就好了。","thinkingSignature":"7aa4ed29b7a6dfb674f52e8d6ea6055b8d74489cd6c6ab5e2ea4326220cd1b75"},{"type":"text","text":"频哥好！我这边准备好了 🍎\n\n麻烦让女儿把英语单元测试的图片发过来——可以是题目照片或者已经答完的试卷都行。发过来之后我帮她：\n\n1. **批改客观题**（阅读理解、完形填空、单项选择等）\n2. **分析错题**（找出知识点漏洞）\n3. **给出建议**（接下来怎么补）\n\n直接发图片就行，我收到就开始～ 📝"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":4139,"output":156,"cacheRead":30974,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":35269,"cost":{"input":0.0012416999999999999,"output":0.0001872,"cacheRead":0.0018584399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0032873399999999997}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774784388441,"responseId":"0618428418404a2107fa90a434d38468"}}
{"type":"message","id":"8fff7eac","parentId":"65d48b2f","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:40:11.563Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[media attached: /Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/8b2ab802-4dbe-4257-9142-462d25c60c77.jpg (image/jpeg) | /Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/8b2ab802-4dbe-4257-9142-462d25c60c77.jpg]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Avoid absolute paths (MEDIA:/...) and ~ paths — they are blocked for security. Keep caption in the text body.\nSystem: [2026-03-29 19:40:10 GMT+8] Feishu[default] DM | 用户612847 (ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83) [msg:om_x100b53a4b74058a0c4967a1acc8ff5f, image, 1 attachment(s)]\n\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b53a4b74058a0c4967a1acc8ff5f\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83\",\n  \"sender\": \"用户612847\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sun 2026-03-29 19:40 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"用户612847 (ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83\",\n  \"name\": \"用户612847\"\n}\n```\n\n/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/8b2ab802-4dbe-4257-9142-462d25c60c77.jpg"}],"timestamp":1774784411560}}
{"type":"message","id":"c497bd91","parentId":"8fff7eac","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:40:18.535Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the image to see the English test paper.","thinkingSignature":"373235c255d20431d865bd6296b706358e69506cfcb079b0df7f74afddc4b6bd"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_tjl7gnwtiez8_1","name":"image","arguments":{"prompt":"请仔细识别这张英语试卷图片的内容，完整还原所有题目和选项内容，特别是：1. 所有客观题的题目、选项、答案；2. 如果有主观题答案或学生作答内容也请识别；3. 图片中任何文字都不要遗漏。","image":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/8b2ab802-4dbe-4257-9142-462d25c60c77.jpg"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":133,"cacheRead":32738,"cacheWrite":2272,"totalTokens":35270,"cost":{"input":0.0000381,"output":0.0001596,"cacheRead":0.0019642799999999997,"cacheWrite":0.000852,"total":0.0030139799999999994}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774784411567,"responseId":"0618429bf3f9a782a50b1ec8d6eb80da"}}
{"type":"message","id":"94431a6d","parentId":"c497bd91","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:40:54.517Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_tjl7gnwtiez8_1","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"这张图片是一张英语试卷的一部分，包含“完型填空”和“阅读”两个部分。以下是完整的文字还原，包括题目、选项以及图片中的手写答案标记。\n\n---\n\n### 完型填空\n\nWe often think humans are special because we can show many emotions. But bumblebees can do this \\_\\_\\_1\\_\\_\\_. They can feel happiness and even spread it to other bees.\n\nA study in *Science* found that good moods can spread, even among insects with brains smaller than a sesame seed (芝麻籽). Scientists gave one bee a surprise treat of sugar water. This made the bee feel happy and change its \\_\\_\\_2\\_\\_\\_. The study showed that it became braver, \\_\\_\\_3\\_\\_\\_ to land on different types of flowers. It also did this more quickly than before. Other bees nearby also began acting more joyfully and bravely, \\_\\_\\_4\\_\\_\\_ they didn't get any sugar water.\n\nTo make sure that the bees weren't just following each other, researchers used barriers (障碍物) to \\_\\_\\_5\\_\\_\\_ how bees were together. This way, bees only used certain \\_\\_\\_6\\_\\_\\_ like touch and sight—or none at all. They found that bees could spread happiness just by seeing each other.\n\nThis is called “positive affective cognition (情感认知)”. It shows the ability to \\_\\_\\_7\\_\\_\\_ others' feelings, which is usually seen in animals with bigger brains. We didn't know bees could do this \\_\\_\\_8\\_\\_\\_ this study.\n\nThis discovery is important. It suggests that sharing emotions is not just for big-brained animals but a key part of social life itself. It also gives us a reason to be \\_\\_\\_9\\_\\_\\_ of our growing understanding of nature.\n\nSo, when you see a bee moving around in the garden, it might be spreading more than just \\_\\_\\_10\\_\\_\\_ it could be spreading joy!\n\n#### 题目选项（包含括号内手写的答案字母）：\n\n( **B** ) 1. A. without brains &emsp; B. as well &emsp; C. by accident  \n( **A** ) 2. A. behaviour (行为) &emsp; B. environment &emsp; C. weight  \n( **C** ) 3. A. pretending &emsp; B. forgetting &emsp; C. daring  \n( **B** ) 4. A. only if &emsp; B. even though &emsp; C. so that  \n( **A** ) 5. A. control &emsp; B. repeat &emsp; C. express  \n( **C** ) 6. A. standards &emsp; B. players &emsp; C. senses  \n( **B** ) 7. A. Hurt &emsp; B. understand &emsp; C. avoid  \n( **A** ) 8. A. until &emsp; B. after &emsp; C. since  \n( **C** ) 9. A. tired &emsp; B. afraid &emsp; C. proud  \n( **B** ) 10. A. stroke &emsp; B. pollen &emsp; C. pepper  \n\n---\n\n### 阅读\n\n“New year is coming!” In a few days, we will welcome the Chinese New Year of Yisi Snake on January 29th. This new year has something special compared with other years: China's Spring Festival was added to the UNESCO Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity (联合国教科文组织人类非物质文化遗产代表作名录) on December 4th, 2024. It includes all the customs of the Spring Festival that Chinese people have been celebrating for thousands of years. So far, the total number of China's Intangible Cultural Heritage on the list has come to the first place in the world.\n\nThis exciting news makes the coming Spring Festival and the Gala more meaningful. We always watch the Gala on the New Year's Eve with our family. The theme of this year's gala is “Year of the Snake, Keep Your Spirits Awake”. And we..."}],"details":{"model":"minimax/MiniMax-VL-01","image":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/media/inbound/8b2ab802-4dbe-4257-9142-462d25c60c77.jpg","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774784454512}}
{"type":"message","id":"7afee039","parentId":"94431a6d","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:41:13.863Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The image shows an English test paper with two sections:\n1. 完型填空 (Cloze test) - 10 questions about bumblebees and emotions\n2. 阅读 (Reading comprehension) - about Chinese New Year and UNESCO\n\nThe user has marked the answers in the image (handwritten letters). Let me identify the answers they marked:\n\n完型填空:\n1. B\n2. A (behaviour)\n3. C (daring)\n4. B (even though)\n5. A (control)\n6. C (senses)\n7. B (understand)\n8. A (until)\n\n\n9. C (proud)\n10. B (pollen)\n\nLooking at the reading comprehension section, it appears to be cut off mid-sentence about the Gala theme, so I'll need to see the complete passage to identify the answers there. The rest of the reading about the Snake year theme seems to continue beyond what's visible in the image, so I'll need to work with just what's provided. I should focus on grading the cloze passage answers since that's where the student has marked responses, then note what I can identify from the reading comprehension portion that's visible. Looking at the answer key for the cloze passage, I'm checking each of the student's marked responses against the correct answers to identify where they went wrong.\n\nFor questions 1 through 7, most of the student's answers were correct—only question 3 about \"daring\" versus \"pretending\" was marked incorrect. I need to continue reviewing the remaining questions to complete the grading summary and provide feedback on common errors or patterns. the reading section appears to be cut off. Let me focus on what I can actually grade - the cloze section where I have clear answers to work with.","thinkingSignature":"02a442b385d8ad3eca71bc8c362283ed4bef5248f67914fb1814600abc828ada"},{"type":"text","text":"图片收到了，正在批改——\n\n---\n\n## 📋 完型填空批改结果（10题）\n\n| 题号 | 女儿答案 | 正确答案 | ❌❌ |\n|------|---------|---------|-----|\n| 1 | B | B | ✅ |\n| 2 |