{"type":"message","id":"0e13d2c7","parentId":"968dc739","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:01:52.730Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the gateway is running. Let me check the Feishu channel configuration to understand the token situation. The issue is that the user's access token has expired and needs to be refreshed. The authorization card should be appearing but isn't.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe I should check the feishu configuration to see if I can understand the token state, or try using the `feishu_oauth` tool to initiate the authorization flow.\n\nActually, thinking about it more - the feishu_oauth tool with action=revoke is only for revoking, not for requesting auth. The authorization card should be sent automatically when a tool fails with an expired token. But it's not appearing.\n\nOne possible reason: maybe the Feishu plugin's user token store has expired and the system can't auto-refresh. In that case, the user needs to go through the OAuth flow again. \n\n\nLet me check the diagnostics endpoint to see what's actually stored for this user.","thinkingSignature":"9b4c7b96d4c63e2c51f618f2756302e0b9cb513abde3506800ef1b5dc8aa2cfe"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_so3l3ffepbcj_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"http://127.0.0.1:18789/api/plugins/feishu-oapi/status\" 2>/dev/null | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null | head -50"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":26082,"output":270,"cacheRead":30974,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57326,"cost":{"input":0.0078246,"output":0.00032399999999999996,"cacheRead":0.0018584399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010007039999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774785703042,"responseId":"061847a7e04f6d2e16c6dc8426171ac8"}}
