{"type":"message","id":"30430889","parentId":"c96a8907","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:02:00.201Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me try another approach. Let me look at the token store directly in the keychain to understand the structure, and see if maybe there's a refresh token that can be used.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The problem is the user access token (UAT) has expired. The OpenClaw Feishu plugin should be automatically handling token refresh. But it seems like the token in the keychain is expired too.\n\nLet me look at the actual keychain entries to see if there's a refresh token.","thinkingSignature":"c08c0c6e6f341c7124fe03a8415e6a5f98e97ab5d175e08c0003bf9fe2a3a303"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_gw1yiez7n8o9_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"security find-generic-password -s \"openclaw-feishu-uat\" -a \"cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83\" -w 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('accessToken:', d.get('accessToken','N/A')[:30]+'...'); print('refreshToken:', d.get('refreshToken','N/A')[:30]+'...' if d.get('refreshToken') else 'N/A')\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":26370,"output":259,"cacheRead":30974,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57603,"cost":{"input":0.007911,"output":0.00031079999999999997,"cacheRead":0.0018584399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010080239999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774785712877,"responseId":"061847b1d47952aa19264d4822986078"}}
