{"type":"message","id":"b5e2e57b","parentId":"03dca5ab","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:02:27.543Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, I'm getting an error about the app access token. This is because I need to use the app access token (not the user access token) to refresh the user token. Let me first get an app access token, then use that to refresh the user token.\n\nActually wait - the refresh token endpoint for user tokens should use the app credentials. Let me re-read the Feishu docs.\n\nActually looking at the Feishu docs, to refresh a user access token, you need:\n- grant_type=refresh_token\n- refresh_token=<the refresh token>\n- client_id=<app_id>\n- client_secret=<app_secret>\n\nBut the error says \"app access token passed is invalid\" - this might mean the endpoint expects an app_access_token as a header, not as a parameter. \n\nLet me try getting an app access token first, then using that to refresh the user token.","thinkingSignature":"a0ade3424bc94d245be989cecd5711259a4a6a978946b9df65bc67aa16398f60"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_12b95czxjh1p_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"APP_ID=\"cli_a93534f5edb85bd3\"\nAPP_SECRET=\"6164wgLUMqlyGbIu9DXzq3Y8\"\n\n# Get app access token first\nAPP_TOKEN_RESULT=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/app_access_token/internal\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d \"{\\\"app_id\\\":\\\"$APP_ID\\\",\\\"app_secret\\\":\\\"$APP_SECRET\\\"}\")\n\necho \"App token result:\"\necho \"$APP_TOKEN_RESULT\" | python3 -m json.tool"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":27441,"output":328,"cacheRead":30974,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":58743,"cost":{"input":0.0082323,"output":0.00039359999999999997,"cacheRead":0.0018584399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010484339999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774785737944,"responseId":"061847ca7679edef4309f75231f99380"}}
