{"type":"message","id":"f35ebfbe","parentId":"f7e3bae2","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:03:03.130Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No relevant logs. Let me think about this differently.\n\nThe issue is:\n1. User access token is expired\n2. App secret in config is invalid (code 10014)\n3. Therefore OpenClaw can't refresh the token automatically\n4. The auth card that should appear automatically isn't appearing\n\nThe user needs to re-authorize manually. But since the automatic flow isn't working, they might need to do something manually.\n\nActually, let me look at the feishu_doctor command - the docs say to use it when \"多次授权仍失败、自动授权无法解决等\". Maybe running this diagnostic would help identify the issue. But this command needs to be sent as a user message in Feishu.\n\nLet me suggest the user try sending `/feishu_doctor` in the chat to see what it shows. This is a diagnostic command that should be handled by the Feishu plugin.\n\nActually wait - let me re-read the error. When I called the refresh token endpoint, I got \"app access token passed is invalid\" (code 20014). But when I tried to get an app access token, I got \"app secret invalid\" (code 10014). This suggests the app secret in the config IS invalid - it might have been changed or rotated on the Feishu developer console.\n\nBut here's the thing - if the app secret is invalid, then the entire Feishu integration should be broken, not just the token refresh. Yet we've been successfully making API calls all evening (uploading images, creating bitable records, etc.) - those were working fine until just now.\n\nWait - let me check when the token actually expired. Maybe the earlier successful API calls were using a cached/valid token, and then it finally gave out.\n\nActually, looking at the timeline:\n- 19:40 - First image (完形填空) - successfully processed\n\n\n- 19:44 - Second image (Unit 3) - successfully uploaded to bitable\n- 19:48 - Third image (词性转换) - successfully uploaded to bitable  \n- 19:52 - Fourth image (企鹅+蜜蜂) - first token expiration error\n- 19:58 - Attempt to upload 企鹅图片 - token still expired\n\nSo the token was working fine for the first few images but expired by the fourth one. This suggests the token might have been manually invalidated or the app secret was rotated after those initial successful calls.\n\nThe real issue is that the Feishu OAuth implementation doesn't support token refresh without user intervention - the plugin requires explicit re-authorization when tokens expire. I need to be upfront with the user that the app credentials appear to have changed or been revoked, and they'll need to go through the authorization flow again.","thinkingSignature":"a8e548495574220a3def1d1ed0c86831b9f2ca9468064731fa28e36cb0f4ba1d"},{"type":"text","text":"频哥，情况有点复杂——\n\n我刚才手动检查发现存在一个问题：\n\n**应用凭证（appSecret）似乎已经失效了**（返回\"app secret invalid\"），所以 OpenClaw 无法自动刷新 token。\n\n这可能是飞书开放平台那边更新了应用的凭证，但没有同步到本地配置。\n\n**解决办法**：需要在飞书开放平台重新获取 appSecret，然后更新到 OpenClaw 的配置里。\n\n你们今天是怎么配置的？之前申请过新的 appSecret 吗？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":28256,"output":661,"cacheRead":30974,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":59891,"cost":{"input":0.0084768,"output":0.0007932,"cacheRead":0.0018584399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01112844}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774785761298,"responseId":"061847e1bcdfa183edd0136d2805cd22"}}
