{"type":"message","id":"dec4218d","parentId":"22fdc8e6","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:03:33.893Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user just sent \"?\" - they seem confused about my previous message. Let me reconsider. Maybe I was wrong about the appSecret being invalid - the error might have been about something else. Let me try a different approach to refresh the token. Actually, let me try the Feishu batch_auth tool again or see if there's another way.\n\nWait - the feishu_oauth_batch_auth returned \"账号 default 缺少 appId 或 appSecret 配置\" - that suggests the tool itself doesn't have access to the credentials even though openclaw.json has them.\n\nLet me check what credentials are actually available to the tools. Maybe the issue is that the tools use a different config source.\n\nActually, thinking about this differently - maybe the token IS refreshed but the API call I made used the wrong endpoint or parameters. Let me try a simpler approach: just re-read the keychain and see if there's a fresh token there now.","thinkingSignature":"182b2aad41949975c49a024326505bfb652367355518da651c6c965109d91e1d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_37tm2ynr00pz_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check current token status\nTOKEN_DATA=$(security find-generic-password -s \"openclaw-feishu-uat\" -a \"cli_a93534f5edb85bd3:ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83\" -w 2>/dev/null)\necho \"Token data length: ${#TOKEN_DATA}\"\n\n# Try to get a fresh token using the refresh token\nREFRESH_TOKEN=$(echo \"$TOKEN_DATA\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('refreshToken',''))\")\n\nAPP_ID=\"cli_a93534f5edb85bd3\"\nAPP_SECRET=\"6164wgLUMqlyGbIu9DXzq3Y8\"\n\n# Get app access token first\nAPP_TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/app_access_token/internal\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d \"{\\\"app_id\\\":\\\"$APP_ID\\\",\\\"app_secret\\\":\\\"$APP_SECRET\\\"}\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('app_access_token',''))\")\n\necho \"App access token: ${APP_TOKEN:0:20}...\"\n\n# Now refresh user token\nif [ -n \"$REFRESH_TOKEN\" ]; then\n  USER_TOKEN_RESULT=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/authen/v1/oidc/refresh_access_token\" \\\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n    -H \"Authorization: Bearer $APP_TOKEN\" \\\n    -d \"grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=$REFRESH_TOKEN&client_id=$APP_ID&client_secret=$APP_SECRET\")\n  echo \"Refresh result: $USER_TOKEN_RESULT\"\nfi"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":607,"cacheRead":30974,"cacheWrite":26520,"totalTokens":58228,"cost":{"input":0.0000381,"output":0.0007283999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0018584399999999998,"cacheWrite":0.009945,"total":0.01256994}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774785794589,"responseId":"0618480222562623d2e5a6f870dec763"}}
