{"type":"message","id":"0f78d1d9","parentId":"c97869b5","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:04:25.406Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The refresh token is also expired or invalid. The user needs to re-authorize the app. But the issue is that the authorization card isn't showing up. \n\nLet me think about what the feishu_oauth_batch_auth tool does and why it failed with \"缺少 appId 或 appSecret 配置\". Maybe the tool uses a different config source.\n\nActually, looking at the error from feishu_oauth_batch_auth: \"账号 default 缺少 appId 或 appSecret 配置\" - this means when the tool runs, it can't find the appId/appSecret in its own config. But they ARE in openclaw.json. Perhaps the tool reads from a different config file.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to trigger the authorization differently. Actually, the user mentioned they don't see the authorization card. In Feishu, OAuth authorization typically happens through a card with a button. If the user isn't seeing it, it might be because:\n\n\n1. The authorization was already completed previously (but tokens expired)\n2. The card is being blocked or not rendered properly\n3. The message was sent but the user didn't see it\n\nI could try sending a direct message to the user with an authorization link, or check if there are any existing messages in the chat that might contain the authorization card but weren't visible to the user.","thinkingSignature":"c150f3bf015fee8582cd450ac000611e27a0f5b38e9dae6cd0e36b99ac7d4a68"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_f7mxhrad66gy_1","name":"feishu_im_user_get_messages","arguments":{"open_id":"ou_2ad19bb3863e71e2d0eff5cc4aeedd83","page_size":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":28919,"output":330,"cacheRead":30974,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":60223,"cost":{"input":0.0086757,"output":0.000396,"cacheRead":0.0018584399999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01093014}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774785